deb file:///opt/phantomos-build/pool ./
#
# Why this deb line is the FIRST line of the file, and why that is not a style choice.
# live-build does not let apt read this file to decide what to mount; its own extractor
# decides, and the extractor reads one line:
#
#   /usr/lib/live/build/chroot_archives:67  Chroot_try_bind_path_from_list
#   functions/chroot_bind_path.sh:63-72     URI=$(sed --regexp-extended \
#                                             -e 's/.*(file:\/\/[^ ]+).*/\1/' ${FILE} | head -1)
#
# `head -1` after the sed, so the *first* line of the file is the only line examined for a
# file: URI. A comment block above the deb line yields the comment's own text as $URI, the
# ^file://(localhost)?/ test fails, no bind mount happens, and apt then correctly reports the
# pool as missing. Measured twice, both times by a failed build: logs/M1-lb-build-pool-order.log
# and logs/M1-lb-build-first-line.log, and the unit control in
# logs/M1-pool-bind-first-line.txt. scripts/build-packages.sh checks line 1, not just
# presence, for exactly this reason.
#
# Why /opt and not /var/tmp, which is where this pool used to live. A bound archive is
# visible inside the chroot at the same absolute path, and live-build's default hooks clean
# the chroot after the packages are installed:
#
#   8070-remove-temporary-files.hook.chroot:6-12
#       for _DIRECTORY in /tmp /var/tmp; do rm -rf ${_DIRECTORY}; mkdir -p …; chmod 1777 …
#
# rm -rf recurses *through* the bind, so that hook deleted the pool's contents at their
# source on the build host and then failed to remove the mountpoint itself — EBUSY, non-zero
# exit, build aborted (logs/M1-lb-build-pool-hook.log:5842-5844, §9.1). The directory-level
# removals across the whole default normal-hook set are /tmp, /var/tmp, /var/cache/man/* and
# /var/cache/ldconfig; the pool path must not be under any of them.
#
# Flat repository — no dists/ tree and no Suite, because the pool is a directory of
# metapackages, not a distribution. Three slashes after file: are load-bearing: the bind only
# matches ^file://(localhost)?/, so file:/opt/... is read as a URI that is not a local path
# and nothing is mounted (functions/chroot_bind_path.sh:18-37).
#
# Verification comes from the matching phantomos.key.chroot, which live-build installs into
# the chroot's /etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d. This line deliberately carries no [trusted=yes], so
# an unsigned pool fails the build instead of shipping. See §9.1 for the signed / wrong-key /
# unsigned measurements.
#
# The bind, not a copy: live-build mounts this host directory into the chroot at the same
# absolute path before its first apt-get update, and the chroot_archives remove step
# unmounts it, deletes this sources entry (chroot_archives:360-366) and deletes the installed
# key (:398-409), then runs apt-get update again with only the shipped channels (:475). So
# §8's "no dead channel in a shipped image" is live-build's own behaviour here rather than a
# cleanup step of ours — and scripts/m1-diff.sh asserts the absence on the built tree rather
# than relying on the comment.
#
# Build-time only: nothing here is a PhantomOS apt channel on a running machine. §12 item 3
# decides where a real one lives; until then a shipped image has no PhantomOS source at all,
# which is what §8 requires rather than an HTTP or unsigned one.
